{"lessons":[{"lesson":"When the weekly quota pacing holds back a wake whose awaited jobs have already ended, raise an alert on the watch page after two hours and name the pacing as the cause in the report, because here it silently refused every wake from about midnight to 16:30 on the first day of the quota week while the next 20-minute evals were ready, and the report blamed idling with work outstanding.","for":"tooling","evidence":"The campaign idled 16.3 h of its 47.0 h window (34%)"},{"lesson":"Before arming, run each decision gate once on the recorded files it will judge and rewrite any gate those files show can never be met, such as a per-seed 'equal' band of ±2 pt when one seed's 95% interval is already 4.4 to 5.3 pt wide, or a 'within 2 pt under every scoring' rule that exact match breaks on every large gain, so the owner is not asked to redefine a gate in the middle of the run.","for":"template","evidence":"one seed's 95% CI on 1,500 Q is .044-.053 wide on"},{"lesson":"Before the tool forwards an owner checkpoint question, have it read the verifier's latest verdicts and either hold the question or attach every claim the verifier downgraded, because here the training checkpoint went to the owner on the claim that all inference work was done, while the slot probes on the finetuned models and the page-transcription control had not run, and the owner closed the campaign on that basis.","for":"tooling","evidence":"arm D moved to Open as incomplete (no finetunes, no transcription control)"},{"lesson":"When the law names data sets for the 'one repeat on new data' rule, check while drafting that their question ids do not overlap the gating set, and where no fresh questions exist, either build and hold back a fresh set before arming or state in the law that a promising document result cannot be repeated.","for":"template","evidence":"gives the same question ids as the gating set (1,500 / 1,500)"},{"lesson":"Make `expmon display` and the result grid read each eval file from the cell's own folder when the law puts every eval behind a linked model folder, so the worker does not have to copy every score in by hand with `expmon probe --from-json`.","for":"tooling","evidence":"`expmon display --exp spread` writes 0 table rows while the grid has judged cells"}]}
